                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have been playing Rotmg since it was released on Steam in 2012 and will do my best to disseminate 3,000 hours without writing an essay\n\nPros:\nGame is constantly changing (for the better (mostly)). DECA is a developer that cares about the state of the game and the quality of the content they release.\n\nThe simple graphics and game play premise (Click to shoot, space bar for your only ability) have been elevated to the highest level of any game I have played. Intricate dungeons, incredible boss fights, and unique builds allow for fun casual gaming but also edge of your seat, throat in your mouth, Discord Raid Leader yelling in your ear type moments. There is nothing like the joy of an epic dungeon White Bag (Best and Rarest loot drop) and the defeat of breaking your headset when you die.\n\nCons:\nMicro transactions do fund the game. They aren't as egregious as they used to be, and you can play totally free and get some paid rewards, but let's not sugarcoat it, if you are really playing, you are going to need (want) to spend money for vault space and a better pet, and it's not a cheap endeavor.\n\nTrading is non-existent, and that really pains me. Back in the day I did more trading in the Nexus (lobby) than playing the actual game itself. Now if there is any gear that's good, you can't trade it. Stat potions used to be the standard currency, but they are so plentiful inflation made them almost worthless. In my opinion, any good MMO should have a trading scene and Realm's died a long time ago\n\nMiddle:\nPerma-Death is a polarizing mechanic, and it is the backbone of Realm. When I was a kid it didn't really bother me that much. Now that I have responsibilities and limited time, it bothers me a lot more. My best friend and I have played this on and off together for 14 years, and those OFF times were ALWAYS associated with someone spending XX hours on a character, dying, and saying you know what I have had enough. This game can bring out the worst in you in an instant all over some colorful pixels\n\nSome have tried to replicate the magic that Realm has somehow kept bottled, but no one has yet to come close. There's a reason that so many people have spent thousands of hours on this game, whether that reason is good or bad is for you to find out.",
